Build passes. Done. Here's what changed:

**gm.html** — 3-column grid replaced with fullscreen `#canvas-area` + 5 floating overlays: topbar (top edge), brush slider (left center), mode toggle (bottom-left), map panel toggle (right center), map panel (right slide-in sheet).

**player.html** — topbar removed. Just `#canvas-area` + `#player-badge` pill in top-left.

**style.css** — complete layout rewrite. Key additions:
- `.floating-control` / `.floating-panel` base classes with `position: fixed`, translucent blur, 8px radius
- All GM controls positioned at edges with 44px+ tap targets
- `#map-panel[hidden]` overrides `display:none` with `display:flex !important` + `translateX(105%)` for CSS slide animation
- Vertical brush slider via `writing-mode: vertical-lr; direction: rtl` (cross-browser)
- Avatar overlap via `margin-left: -8px` + `:first-child { margin-left: 0 }`
- `.removal-overlay` fullscreen blur overlay for removed players
- All home/card styles untouched

**gm.ts** — removed `inviteLinkEl`/`copyInviteBtn` refs; added `connectionStatusEl`, `playerPresenceEl`, `mapPanelToggleBtn`, `mapPanel`; `renderPresence()` with Miro-style avatar stack (online first, max 4 visible, +N overflow); popover with Copy link / Remove per player; map panel toggle; connection status dot updates; `gallery.replaceChildren()` instead of `innerHTML = ''`.

**player.ts** — removed `adventureNameEl` (adventure name in `document.title` only); `player:removed` now shows styled `.removal-overlay` instead of raw `p` element.
